name 'iterating-with-ai-postassessment-q3_2025'

question 'A loop is designed to run from `i = 0` to `i < 5`. If the developer accidentally changes the condition to `i <= 5`, how many times will the loop run?'

wrong '4 times'
wrong '5 times'
right '6 times'
wrong 'It will not run at all.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 2

Using `< 5` runs the loop for 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 (5 times). Using `<= 5` adds an extra iteration for index 5, totaling 6 times. This is a classic "off-by-one" error.
MARKDOWN
